   "researcher_notes": "GEM does not list this data center. Amazon Data Services applied to the Maryland Department of the Environment for an air permit to construct for four data centers called IAD-534 to IAD-537 in Frederick County. The state's March 25, 2026 release says Amazon has applied for an additional Frederick facility, and a public meeting on the IAD-534 campus was held on May 28, 2026. The application and the state's slides list 99 diesel emergency generators, 92 of 2,750 kilowatts, 6 of 750 kilowatts and 1 of 250 kilowatts, 257.75 MW in all. That is far above the 50 MW threshold, so the plant is an add. The application says it is a separate source from Amazon's BWI-150 campus, which is the 3250 Digital Drive plant in the other new record, and the slides place it 0.59 miles away. A tracker site links the application to Rowan's Bauxite II at 3300 Radiant Way, but I did not find that in a state document. No permit has been issued, so the status is announced. I found no exact point, so the point shown is the Quantum campus area and the accuracy is approximate. I found no Public Service Commission exemption case for it.",
